<title>JAPAN: NKK mulls 35 bln yen straight bond issue -- sources.</title>
<headline>NKK mulls 35 bln yen straight bond issue -- sources.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>NKK Corp is considering issuing domestic straight bonds worth about 35 billion yen, underwriting sources said on Monday.</p>
<p>They said the steelmaker is considering issuing the bonds in three tranches.</p>
<p>It is likely to issue about 15 billion yen worth of four-year bonds, 10 billion yen worth of six-year bonds and 10 billion yen worth of eight-year bonds, the sources said.</p>
<p>Some of them said NKK may decide the terms of the issue by the end of this year.</p>
<p>NKK officials declined to comment.</p>
</text>
